; A SIMD-group's xor-butterfly reduction, v' = op(v, shuffle_xor(v, d)) for
; d = 16, 8, 4, 2, 1 in any order (quad shuffles for d <= 2), leaves every
; lane holding the reduction of all 32: one simd reduction. Integer add,
; and, or, xor, min and max are associative and commutative, so the order
; does not change the value. A float add or multiply is the same in the
; hardware's order only: d = 1, 2, 4, 8, 16 (pairs of neighbouring lanes
; first), or the halves-first order over the lanes in bit-reversed order
; (two xor shuffles and selects first); not where NaN results are made
; canonical. Off by default: with many SIMD-groups resident the 23-cycle
; reduction is slower than the butterfly (EXPERIMENTS.md L15-E364).

